.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_RSTATE_STRING 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_rstate_string ,
.Nm SSL_rstate_string_long
.Nd get textual description of state of an SSL object during read operation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft const char *
.Fo SSL_rstate_string
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo SSL_rstate_string_long
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_rstate_string
returns a 2 letter string indicating the current read state of the SSL
object
.Fa ssl .
.Pp
.Fn SSL_rstate_string_long
returns a string indicating the current read state of the SSL object
.Fa ssl .
.Sh NOTES
When performing a read operation, the SSL/TLS engine must parse the
record, consisting of header and body.
When working in a blocking environment,
.Xr SSL_rstate_string[_long] 3
should always return "RD"/"read done".
.Pp
This function should only seldom be needed in applications.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SSL_rstate_string
and
.Fn SSL_rstate_string_long
can return the following values:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqRH"/"read header"
The header of the record is being evaluated.
.It \(dqRB"/"read body"
The body of the record is being evaluated.
.It \(dqunknown"/"unknown"
The read state is unknown.
This should never happen.
.El
.Pp
When used with QUIC SSL objects, these functions always return
"RH"/"read header" in normal conditions.
